base layers.","content_type":"text","element_id":"index-sol-5956f7bf-5b57-416f-89cf-f05c34a5de47-desc"},{"content_value":"<br><div><br></div>","content_type":"text","element_id":"hero-desc-3"},{"content_value":"/images/cms/bg-image/1790976250894_Marine3.webp","content_type":"image","element_id":"hero-bg-3"},{"content_value":"/images/cms/bg-image/1791312359114_FG_Closeup1.webp","content_type":"image","element_id":"hero-bg-1"},{"content_value":"<span style=\"color: rgb(243, 237, 237);\">Geosynthetic<span style=\"font-weight: normal;\"> Soil </span><span style=\"caret-color: rgb(243, 237, 237);\"><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">Stabilization <span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Solutions</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><div><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"></span></div></span><div><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"></span></div>","content_type":"text","element_id":"hero-title"},{"content_value":"Baselok<sup>&reg;</sup> FPS improves the interaction between foundation materials and the underlying soil, creating a reinforced platform that increases bearing capacity and minimizes differential settlement. This results in stronger foundations capable of supporting heavy structural loads even in challenging ground conditions","content_type":"text","element_id":"index-sol-b29a61da-63a1-425b-833c-20bc7f62aea0-desc"},{"content_value":"<div><span style=\"text-align: inherit; letter-spacing: 0.2px; font-size: 13px;\">Collaborative</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0.2px; text-align: inherit; font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;Value Engineering and Site-Specific Design for Contractors and Geotechnical Engineers.</span></div><div><span style=\"text-align: inherit; letter-spacing: 0.2px; font-size: 13px;\">Choosing subgrade stabilization requires balancing performance, cost, and structural reliability. The BaseLok<sup>&reg;</sup></span><span style=\"text-align: inherit; letter-spacing: 0.2px; font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;product line by Industrial Fabrics, Inc. replaces unpredictable ground improvement with mathematically verifiable mechanical stabilization.</span></div><div><span style=\"text-align: inherit; letter-spacing: 0.2px; font-size: 13px;\">To bridge the gap between design and jobsite execution, our dedicated BaseLok</span><span style=\"text-align: inherit; letter-spacing: 0.2px;\"><sup>&nbsp;</sup></span><span style=\"text-align: inherit; letter-spacing: 0.2px; font-size: 13px;\">Engineering Team provides technical consultation and custom design recommendations from project conception through construction.&nbsp;</span></div><div><span style=\"text-align: inherit; letter-spacing: 0.2px; font-size: 13px;\">Our mechanical stabilization guidance provides clear engineering and financial advantages:</span></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\"><li><b><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Eliminate Chemical Stabilization:</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\"> Remove the high cost, environmental liabilities, and mixing complexities associated with traditional lime or cement subgrade treatment.</span></li><li><b><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Reduce Aggregate Thickness:</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\"> Optimize load distribution to decrease necessary aggregate fill volumes, lowering excavation, haul-in, and material costs.</span></li><li><b><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Expedite Construction Timelines:</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\"> Utilize rapid, straightforward installation processes to accelerate your overall project schedule.</span></li><li><b><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Extend Asset Service Life:</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\"> Prevent long-term differential settlement, minimize rut depth, and increase the bearing capacity of roads, railways, and foundations.</span></li></ul></div>","content_type":"text","element_id":"why-desc"},{"content_value":"/images/cms/OTHERS/1791467024124_BLPro_Clear.webp","content_type":"image","element_id":"bpro-global-device"},{"content_value":"Between Biaxial and Uniaxial Geogrid and Cellular Confinement Technologies, Geosynthetics Have Been at the Forefront of Soil Stabilization Applications Since 1959.","content_type":"text","element_id":"footer-tagline"}]